From eb624052a56443bdb8fbc56db34ebab92352692b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsha Nanda <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:32:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] chore: ignore .forge/config.yaml
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The file is written by forge's own config commands, and the protected-state
pre-commit gate blocks hand-commits to it — so a tracked copy can only ever be
stale, and it surfaces as permanent noise in git status on any machine where
forge has run.

This was the one piece of the old local-only master commits that PR #534 did
not carry across.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitignore | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 5ec9d5af..257d503a 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -99,6 +99,10 @@ docs/planning/
 # written by the per-turn recall hook). Machine- and session-specific — never source.
 .forge/memory-recall/
 
+# Managed by `forge` config commands, not by hand — the protected-state gate
+# blocks direct commits, so a tracked copy can only ever be stale.
+.forge/config.yaml
+
 # Protected-state audit log (capped append-only record of blocked protected-path
 # edits, written by the pre-commit check). Machine-local — never source.
 .forge/protected-state-audit.jsonl
-- 
2.51.0.windows.1

